  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Jonathan V. Gould said he would use technology and AI to reach supervisory conclusions faster, deploy examiner resources based on risk, and perform more direct validation of larger banks’ balance sheets and financial risks. Gould said banks had been fortifying their defenses for months and using “SI” as a defense against AI agents. Gould said the federal banking agencies revised model risk management guidance to avoid impeding banks’ use of AI and planned to seek public information on what additional guidance would be helpful.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3"
   ],
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "Jonathan V. Gould said he would use technology and AI to reach supervisory conclusions faster, deploy examiner resources based on risk, and perform more direct validation of larger banks’ balance sheets and financial risks.",
